  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated food security and nutrition response to avert famine and support drought recovery in Somalia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main aim of this $4.5m WFP project is to address the food consumption gap and support drought recovery. To that end, WFP will provide food assistance through cash to 18,000 people, rehabilitate and establish community water structures through cash for assets, create income-generating activities for displaced people, and provide nutrition treatment to children. In total, the food security component targets 26,136 people, including 9,670 women and 3,396 girls. The nutrition component targets 47,997 girls and boys.</narrative>
  </description>
